hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10561","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, narrated by Abu Al-Nadr, narrated by Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed The night of the evening prayer, peace be upon him, then he went out to the mosque and saw the people waiting for the prayer. He said: “It is not one of these religions.” “No one remembers God at this hour except you.” He said: And this verse was revealed: “They are not alike from the People of the Book,” until it was conveyed: “By God.” \Knowing of the righteous\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"10562","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that a servant of Hatib came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining. A wood-cutter, and he said: O Messenger of God, let a wood-cutter enter Hell. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You lied. He will not enter it, for he testified.” \Badr"
"10563","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said “Allahu Akbar” when he raised his head in the morning prayer from the last rak’ah, saying: “O God, curse so-and-so and so-and-so.” He supplicated against some hypocrites. Then God Almighty revealed: You have no say in the matter. Or turn to them or punish them, for they are wrongdoers."
"10564","'Amr ibn al-Harith (said): Mahbub ibn Musa narrated to us, (saying): Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Salim narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he raised his head from bowing (ruku') in the last rak'ah of the Fajr prayer, say—after saying: ""Allah hears him who praises Him, Our Lord, to You belongs all praise""—""O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so."""""
"10565","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, and I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Humaid, he said: He said Anas: The ankle strap of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was broken on the day of Uhud and he was injured, causing blood to flow down his face, and he wiped the blood from his face. And he says: “How can a people succeed who have stained the face of their Prophet while he is calling them to Islam?” Then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: You have no say in the matter. anything, or turn to them in repentance, or punish them, for they are wrongdoers.” The wording is by Khalid. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10566","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Abu Awanah, on the authority of Othman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Asma bin Al-Hakam Al-Fazari, he said : I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: I was a man when I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hadith from which God would benefit me, including He wanted to benefit me, so if one of his companions spoke to me, I made him swear to him, and if he swore to me, I told him the truth. Abu Bakr told me, and Abu told the truth. Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no man who commits a sin and then gets up and purifies himself.” So he purifies himself well, then asks forgiveness from God, Blessed and Most High, unless He forgives him.” Then he recited this verse: And those who, if they commit an indecent act or They wronged themselves, until the end of the verse.”"
"10567","Hilal bin Al-Ala, narrated by Husayn bin Ayyash, narrated by Zuhayr, narrated by Abu Ishaq, told me: I heard Al-Baraa bin `Aazib, speaking, he said: He made The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked the archers on the day of Uhud, and they were fifty men, Abdullah bin Jubayr, he said: He placed them in a place, and said To them: “If you see us being snatched up by birds, do not depart from this place of yours until I send for you. If you see us, we will defeat the people.” And We gave them rest, so do not depart until I send for you.” He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and those with him walked, and he defeated them. By God, I saw the women climbing the mountain, their anklets visible, and their legs were lifting up their clothes. The companions of Abdullah bin Jubayr: The spoils, meaning collect the spoils. Your friends have appeared, so what are you waiting for? Abdullah bin Jubair said: Have you forgotten what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to you? They said: By God, we will go to the people and get our share of the spoils. When they came to them, their faces were turned away, so they came back defeated. That was when The Messenger called them at the end, but only twelve men remained with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They killed seventy of us, and there were The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions captured one hundred and forty of the polytheists on the Day of Badr: seventy prisoners, and seventy killed, so he said Abu Sufyan: Is there Muhammad among the people? Is there Muhammad among the people? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade them to answer him, then he said: Is Ibn Abi Quhafa among the people? Three times, he said: Is Ibn Al-Khattab among the people? Three times, then he returned to his companions and said: As for these people, they have been killed. Omar could not control himself, so he said: You lied, O enemy of God. You have prepared for all of them to be alive, and there remains for you what will harm you. He said: One day after the day of Badr, and the wars are a dispute. You will see among the people For example, I did not order it, and you did not please me. Then he began to tremble, saying, “Is it stupid?” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Won’t you answer him?” They said: O Messenger of God, what should we say? He said: “Say: God is Most High and Most Majestic.” He said: “We have Uzza, and you have no Uzza.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you not answer him?” They said: O Messenger of God, what should we say? He said: “Say: God is our Master and He is not your Master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10568","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna. He said: Na Khalid, Na Humaid. Anas said: Abu Talha said: “I was among those who made him sleepy on the day of Uhud until he fell asleep.” The sword is from my hand three times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10569","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, and Harun bin Abdullah, they said: Our name is Yahya bin Abi Bukair, I am Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abi Husayn, on the authority of Abi Ad-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The last words of Abraham, peace be upon him, when he was thrown into the fire were: God suffices me, and He is good.” Al-Wakeel, he said: And your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something like it: Those to whom the people said, “The people have gathered against you, so fear them.” So it increased their faith and they said, “Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10570","I am Ismail bin Yaqoub bin Ismail, narrated by Ibn Musa, narrated by my father, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and he mentioned a chain of narration. Another, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “How blessed he was, when the one who made the pictures looked up at the horn and listened with his hearing and bowed his forehead.” He waits when he is commanded and blows it.” They said: O Messenger of God, how do we say? He said: “Say: God is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs. In God we trust.”"
"10571","I am Muhammad bin Mansour, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: “When the polytheists departed from Uhud, And they reached the spirits, and they said: You did not kill Muhammad, nor did you attack the Ka'ab, but wretched is what you did, return. So that was conveyed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. So the people mourned, and they mourned until they reached Hamra al-Asad and Bir Abi Utaiba. Then God Almighty revealed: Those who responded. To God and the Messenger after the affliction afflicted them, and Abu Sufyan had said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Your appointment is the season of Badr, where You killed our companions, but as for the cowardly one, he returned, and as for the brave man, he took up the skill of fighting and trading, but they did not find anyone with him, so he descended. God Almighty: So they returned by the grace of God and His bounty, and no harm touched them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10572","I am Mujahid bin Musa, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Jami` bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “There is no man who has wealth who does not pay what is owed to him except that a brave and strong man is placed around his neck, and he will flee from him and he will follow him.” He said: Then he read its authenticity from the Book of God: “And do not think that those who are miserly will mention His saying: On the Day of Resurrection.”"
"10573","I am Muhammad bin Hatim bin Naim, I am Suwayd, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God Blessed and Most High said: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no danger has come to. The heart of a human being, and if you wish, recite: No soul knows what has been hidden from them of the comfort of eyes.” And he said: “In Paradise there is a tree on which the rider may travel.” In its shade is one hundred years, so read: And an extended shade, and the place of a whip in Paradise is better than this world and all that is in it, so read: So whoever moves away away from the Fire and entered into Paradise. He has already succeeded, and the life of this world is nothing but the enjoyment of deception.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10574","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, narrated by Hajjaj, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, and I am Yusuf bin Saeed, narrated by Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi told me Malika, that Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf told him that Marwan said: Go, O Rafi, to his gatekeeper, to Ibn Abbas. So say: If every one of us was happy with what he did and loved to be praised for what he did, he would be punished, we would certainly be punished all together. Ibn Abbas said: “ What do you have to do with this verse? This was only revealed about the People of the Book. Then Ibn Abbas recited: And when God took a covenant from those who were given the Book So that you may make it clear to the people, and Ibn Abbas recited: Do not think that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they did not do, Ibn Abbas said. Abbas: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked them about something, but they concealed it, and they told him something else, so they went out and were happy that they had told him something. He asked them about him, and they were grateful to him for that, and they rejoiced in what they had achieved by concealing from him what he asked them about.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10575","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, that Ibn Abbas told him, He spent the night at the house of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was his maternal aunt, so I lay on the width of the pillow, and the Messenger of God lay down. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his family during its entire period. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slept until midnight, or a little before it. Or shortly after that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, wiping the sleep from his face, then he recited the last ten verses from Surah Al Imran, then he got up to a hanging hanger, performed his ablution from it, then stood up to pray. Ibn Abbas said: So I got up and did the same as he did. So I went and stood next to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his right hand on my head and began to twist it by my ear. So he prayed two rak'ahs, then two more rak'ahs, then two more rak'ahs, then two more rak'ahs, then two more rak'ahs, then two more rak'ahs, then he prayed Witr, and he lay down until The muezzin came to him, then he got up and prayed two rak’ahs, then he went out and prayed the Fajr prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10576","I am Amr bin Mansour, I am Yazid bin Mihran, we are Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: “When the obituary of the Negus came, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray for him.” They said: O Messenger of God, shall we pray for an Ethiopian slave? Then God Almighty revealed: And indeed, from the People of the Book is he who believes in God and in what has been revealed to you, and in what was sent down to them, they are submissive.” I am Amr bin Mansour, na Yazid bin Mahran. Abu Khaled Al-Kabbaz, I am Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, similar to him"
"10577","I am Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif, from Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, from my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa bin told me Al-Zubayr said that he asked Aisha: About the words of God Almighty: “And if you fear that you will not be just towards orphans, then marry as many women as please you.” Three and a quarter times, she said: O son of my sister, she is an orphan in the custody of her guardian, sharing her wealth with him, so he admires her wealth and her beauty. Her guardian wants to marry her without being fair in her friendship, so he gives her the same as what he gives to someone else, so they are forbidden from marrying them unless That they be fair to them, and that they reach their highest age in friendship, so they were commanded to marry whatever women pleased them besides themselves,” Urwah said. Aisha said: Then the people consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after this verse, and God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: And they ask you for a fatwa concerning women. Say, “Allah gives you a fatwa concerning them and what is recited to you in the Book regarding orphan women to whom you do not give what is prescribed for them.” And you wish to marry them, so God mentioned that it was recited to you in the first book. God said: And if you fear that you will not do justice to the orphans. So marry whatever women please you.” Aisha said: And God Almighty says in the other verse: And you desire to marry them, desiring Is one of you talking about his orphan when she was short of money and short of beauty? She said: So they forbade them from marrying someone whose wealth and beauty they desired. “Women are not orphans except with justice because of their desire for them if they are lacking in money and beauty.”"
"10578","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, narrated by Hajjaj Adah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Al-Munkadir informed me, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, visited me.” May God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr were walking among Banu Salamah, and he found that I had no sense, so he called for water and performed ablution, then he sprinkled some of it on me, and I woke up. So I said: What should I do with my money, O Messenger of God? Then God revealed: God enjoins upon you concerning your children: for the male, the share of two females. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10579","I am Ali bin Hajar, this is Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The harm in the will Of the major sins, then he recited: These are the limits of God, and whoever obeys God and His Messenger, He will admit him to Gardens under which rivers flow, to abide therein. And that is the great victory {13} And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger and transgresses His limits - He will admit him to the Fire to abide therein, and for him is a humiliating punishment {14}.”"
"10580","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Take it from me, take it from me. God has made a way for them. The virgin will be flogged for the virgin.” One hundred and one year’s banishment, and the unmarried for the unmarried a hundred lashes and stoning with stones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10581","I am Ahmad bin Harb, on the authority of Asbat, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. Abu Ishaq said: Ata’ Abu mentioned Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in this verse: “O you who have believed, it is not lawful for you to inherit women by force, nor to prevent them from going With some of what you have given them, they said: When a man died, his guardians had more right to his wife. If some of them wished, he could marry her, and if he wished They married her off, for they have more right to her than her family, so this verse was revealed about that.”"
"10582","It is narrated by Ali bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, it is narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Umamah, on the authority of his father, he said: “When Abu Qais died Ibn Al-Asalat wanted his son to marry his wife after him, and that was theirs in pre-Islamic times, so God Almighty revealed: No. It is permissible for you to inherit women by force. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10583","I am Ismail bin Masoud, from Khaled, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abi Alqamah, on the authority of Abi Saeed, He mentioned: “The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, captured captives from the polytheists, and some of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Stop cheating on them for the sake of their husbands, so it was revealed: And the chaste women, except those your right hands possess."
"10584","I am Yahya bin Hakim, we are Muhammad bin Jaafar, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Othman Al-Bati, he said: I heard Abu Al-Khalil speaking, on the authority of Abu Sa’id He said: “They captured captives who had wives, and they had intercourse with each other, as if they were afraid of that, so God Almighty revealed: And chaste women, except those whom your right hands possess.” “I am Yahya bin Hakim, I am Muhammad bin Ja’far, I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10585","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Al-Nadr, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Anas, he said: I heard Anas, saying: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The major sins: associating others with God, disobeying one’s parents, killing oneself, and false speech.”"
"10586","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Baqiyya, we are Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, that Abu Rahm al-Sam’i narrated to him, that Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, narrated to him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever comes to worship God and does not associate anything with Him, and establishes prayer, and performs zakat, and avoids the great sins, for for him is Paradise.” They asked him about the great sins, and he said: “Associating partners with God and killing a Muslim soul.” And fleeing on the day of the advance.”"
"10587","Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim told me: I am Ibn Shumail, I am Shu`bah, I am Firas, he said: I heard al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The great sins: associating partners with God, disobeying one’s parents, killing oneself, and swearing a false oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10588","I am Musa bin Abdul Rahman, from Abu Usama, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ O God, forgive Abdullah bin Qais, strengthen him, and admit him to a noble entrance on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10589","I am Harun bin Abdullah, I am Abu Usama, I am Idris bin Yazid, I am Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas In his saying: “And those to whom your oaths have been made, give them their share.” He said: “When the immigrants came to Medina, the Ansar would inherit without mercy.” For the brothers among whom the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a brotherhood. When the verse was revealed: And for each of us We appointed a guardian from what the parents and relatives have left behind. He said: So I abrogated it. And to those of you whose oaths were confirmed, give them their share of victory, advice, and protection, and a will will be made for him, and the inheritance has gone. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10590","I am Abdah bin Abdullah, I am Yazid, I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Muawiyah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello. A man asked him: What rights does a woman have over her husband? He said: “You feed her when you feed her, and you clothe her when you clothe her, and you do not strike her in the face, and you do not curse her, and you do not leave her except in the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10591","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Ali, who is Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God said to me: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was on the pulpit: “Recite to us.” I said: O Messenger of God, am I reciting to you, but it was only revealed to you? He said: “I would love to hear it from someone else.” So I recited Surat An-Nisa until I reached his statement: So how if We bring from every nation a witness? And We brought you as a witness against these. He winked at me, and I looked and behold, his eyes were sparkling."
"10592","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abu Dawud, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Badimah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated. He said: It was abrogated by: O you who have believed, when you stand up for prayer, wash yourself. \your faces\"""""""
"10593","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali: “The A man from the Ansar invited him and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and he gave them drink before alcohol was forbidden. Then Ali led them in Morocco, so he recited: Say: O you disbelievers! So he mixed it up, so it was revealed: Do not approach prayer while you are drunk until you know what you are saying."
"10594","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “We went out with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, during some of his travels, until we were in Al-Bayda’, or with the same army, a contract with me was broken, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stayed. Peace be upon him upon his request, and the people stayed with him but they were not on water, and they did not have water, so the people came to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and they said: Do you not see what Aisha did? She stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with the people, and they were not on water, and they had no water. Then Abu came Bakr, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell asleep on my thigh, and he said: Did you imprison the Messenger of God and the people while they were not on water, and they had no water with them? She said: Then Abu Bakr blamed me and said, “What God wills him to say,” and he began to stab me in the waist with his hand. Nothing prevented me from moving except a place. The head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rested on my thigh until the morning was without water, and then God Almighty revealed the verse about tayammum: “So perform tayammum,” he said. Usayd bin Hudayr: What is the first blessing of yours, O family of Abu Bakr? He said: So we removed the camel that you were riding and found the knot under it."
"10595","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of Awf, he said: Hayyan narrated to me with Istakhr, on the authority of Qatn bin Qubaisah, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, roads, food, and cleanliness are part of poverty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10596","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, narrated by Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ya’la bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “ O you who have believed, obey God and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. It was revealed about Abdullah bin Hudhafah bin Qais bin Adi Al-Sahmi, When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him on a mission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10597","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, that he narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to him, that a man Al-Zubayr quarreled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, over the annex of the free land with which they used to irrigate the palm trees. The Ansari said: Let the water pass. He refused, so they disputed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Al-Zubayr: “Give water, O Zubayr. Then send to your neighbour.” The Ansari got angry and said: O Messenger of God, if he is your cousin. Then the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, colored. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then he said: “O Zubair, water, then withhold the water until it returns to the walls.” Al-Zubair said: By God, I consider this verse to be true. It was revealed about that: But no, by your Lord, they do not believe."
"10598","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, from Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I had heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not die until he has a choice between this world and the hereafter, so he was seized by hoarseness during the illness in which he died. So I heard him say: “Among those upon whom God has bestowed blessings, among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and those are good companions.” So I thought that He was given a choice (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10599","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: I am my father, he said: I am Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and his companions came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, and they said: O Prophet of God, we We were in glory while we were polytheists, but when we believed we became humiliated. He said: “I have been commanded to pardon, so do not fight the people.” When God turned him into Medina. He ordered fighting, so they refrained, so God Almighty revealed: Have you not seen those to whom it was said, Restrain your hands and establish prayer and give zakat? And when fighting was prescribed for them, a group of them feared the people. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10600","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said In this verse: “What do you have regarding the hypocrites, two groups, when God has made them miserable for what they have earned?” He said: Some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned. And the people were divided into two groups: one group of them said: Kill them, and another group said: No. Then the verse was revealed: So what is the matter with you? The hypocrites are divided into two categories, and he said: It removes impurity, just as fire removes impurity from silver. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10601","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, we are Muhammad, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abza commanded me to... I asked Ibn Abbas about these two verses: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell.” So I asked him, and he said: Nothing abolishes it. And regarding this verse: And those who do not call upon any other god with God, and do not kill a soul that God has forbidden except in a just way. He said: It was revealed about the people of \polytheism\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"10602","I am Azhar bin Jamil, we are Khalid bin Al-Harith, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Numan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The people of Kufa disagreed regarding this verse: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, then I went to Ibn Abbas and asked him, and he said: It was revealed in The last thing that was revealed, nothing abrogated it.”"
"10603","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid. Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Muslims pursued a man in spoils for him, and he said: Peace be upon you. So they killed him and took his spoils, so God Almighty revealed: And do not say to the one who extends peace to you, “You are not Believing, you seek the reward of the life of this world, that is the spoils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10604","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, from Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj. He said: Abd al-Karim told me that he heard Maqsam speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “Those of the believers who are sitting at Badr and those who are going to Badr are not equal,” said Abdul-Rahman bin Jahsh Al-Asadi and Abdullah. He is the son of Umm Maktum. He said: We are blind, O Messenger of God. Do we have a concession? Then it was revealed: Not equal among the believers are those who sit behind, except those in need of harm. To: to those who sit in a degree, for these who are sitting are not deserving of harm: And God has favored the mujahideen over those who sit by a great reward {95} degrees from Him, on Those who sit among the believers, not those deserving of harm.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10605","I am Nasr bin Ali, narrated by Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a word that means He said: “Bring me your shoulder and the inkwell.” So he wrote: Those who sit among the believers are not equal, and Amr bin Umm Maktum was behind him. He said: Is there anyone A license? Then it was revealed: “Not those destined to harm.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10606","I am Zakaria bin Yahya, I am Ishaq, I am Al-Muqri, I am Haywa bin Shurayh, I am Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, he said: It was cut off from the people of Medina. He was sent to Yemen, so I registered for it, and I met Ikrimah, so I informed him. He strictly forbade me from that, and said: Ibn Abbas: “Indeed, some Muslims were with the polytheists, enlarging the numbers of the polytheists, and one of them came and shot an arrow and hit him.” So he kills him, or he strikes him and he is killed. Then it was revealed: Those whom the angels took to death who wronged themselves. They said, “Why were you?” They said, “We were weak.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10607","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Sa’id al-Qattan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Ammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Ya’la bin Umayyah, said: I said to Omar: Shorten the prayer. God Almighty said: If you fear that Those who disbelieved will tempt you, and that has gone away now. He said: I was astonished at what you were astonished at. I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “It is charity that God has given to you, so accept His charity.”"
"10608","I am Ahmad bin Al-Khalil and Al-Abbas bin Muhammad. They said: Hajjaj told us. Ibn Juraij said: Ya’la told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “If you are harmed by rain or are sick,” Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, Ahmad added: He was wounded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10609","I am Abu Bakr bin Ali, on the authority of Yahya bin Muin, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Muhaisn, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When it was revealed: It is not based on your wishes, nor the hopes of the People of the Book, that whoever does evil will be rewarded for it, so make that difficult for the Muslims. So they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him, and he said: “Approach and repel, for for everything that afflicts a servant there is expiation, even the calamity.” He pricks it, and pricks it with a thorn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10610","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Zakaria bin Adi, we are Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith said: Jundub told me that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say five things before he died, saying: “I had some of you.” Brothers and friends, and I disavow every friend of his kinship, and if I were to take a friend from my nation, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a friend. My Lord has taken me as a friend just as He took Abraham as a friend, and do not take graves as places of worship, for I forbid you from that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10611","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Isa bin Yunus, from Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, in his saying: “And they ask you for a fatwa about women. Say, ‘God. He gives you a fatwa concerning them and what is recited to you in the Book regarding orphan women whom you do not give. She said: It was revealed about the orphan girl that she may be with the man, perhaps she That she has shared his money with him and he is her guardian, so he desires to marry her, but he hates to marry her to a man and share with him his money. Because of what she shared with him, then he will reward her, so God Almighty and Majestic revealed: And they will ask you for a fatwa concerning women."
"10612","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abu Muawiyah, we are Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, in the Almighty’s saying: “And if a woman fears From her husband is disobedience or abandonment. It was revealed about a woman. It is with a man. He does not take too much of her, so he wants to divorce her and marry someone else. So you say: Do not divorce me, but keep me and you are free from maintenance and division for me. So God Almighty revealed: So there is no blame on them if they make amends. peace between them.”"
"10613","I am Ali bin Hajar, from Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Woe to the one who talks and lies and the people laugh at him. Woe to him, woe to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10614","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Abu Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “There are three signs of a hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies, when he is trusted, he betrays, and when he makes a promise, he breaks it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10615","This is Muhammad bin Salamah, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Al-Harith bin Hisham, asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: O Messenger of God, how does the revelation come to you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell, and it is the hardest on me, so it is separated from me, and I have become aware of it.” He did not say, “And sometimes the angel appears to me as a man and speaks to me, and I understand what he says.” Aisha said: “And I saw him descend upon him on a difficult day.” cold, and he is relieved of it, and his forehead is covered with sweat. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10616","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is not a prophet among the prophets but that he has been given signs similar to him. Humans have believed in him, but it was only what I was given a revelation that God revealed to me. “I hope that I will be the most follower of them on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10617","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Protest Adam and Moses. Moses said to Adam: You are the one whom God created with His own hand and breathed into you of His Spirit. You deceived people and expelled them from Paradise. So he said Adam: You are the one whom God chose with His message and spoke to you in a precise way. Do you blame me to do a work that God prescribed for me before He created the heavens? And the earth, so Adam performed Hajj with Moses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10618","I am Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, on the authority of Hammad, narrated by Ma’abad bin Hilal, who said: A group of the people of Basra gathered, so we set off for Anas. Ibn Malik, so we found him while he was praying the noon prayer, so we waited until he finished, so we entered upon him, and he sat still on his bed, and he said to him: Oh Abu Hamza, our brothers are asking you about the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding intercession. Anas said: Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “When on the Day of Resurrection people will gather among themselves, then Adam will be brought, and it will be said to him: O Adam, intercede for your offspring. So he says: I am not hers, but you are responsible for Abraham, for he is the friend of the Most Gracious. So Abraham is brought, and he says, meaning: I am not hers, but you are upon me. Through Moses, he is the speaker of God. Then Moses is brought, and he says: I am not for it, but you should go to Jesus, for he is the spirit and word of God, so Jesus, peace be upon him, is brought. So he says: I am not hers, but you must go to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he is brought, and I say: I am hers, so I ask permission from my Lord. Then the call is given to me, so I stand before him, and he inspires me with praises that I cannot do now, so I praise him with those praises, then I prostrate before him. So He says: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, and intercede and you will be interceded. So I say: Oh Lord, my nation, my nation. It is said: Go, who will In his heart he either said: A weight of righteousness or a strand of faith, so take him out of it, then I will go and do it, then I will come back and praise. With those words of Muhammad, then he prostrated to him again, and it is said: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be interceded, so I say: O Lord, my nation, my nation. Then it will be said: Go, and whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, take him out of it. Then I will go and do it. Then I return and praise with those words of praise, then I fall back and prostrate before him, and it is said to me: O Muhammad, raise your head, and speak and it will be heard, and ask and it will be given to you. And intercede, and you will be interceded. Then I will say: O Lord, my nation, my nation. Then it will be said: Go. And whoever has in his heart anything less than the weight of a mustard seed, Then take him out of the fire, and he will go.” Narrated by Anas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10619","Mahmoud bin Khalid, narrated to me by Umar, meaning Ibn Abd al-Wahid, told me on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Umair bin Hani, Junada bin Abu Umayyah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad His servant and Messenger, and that Jesus is the servant of God and His word which He bestowed upon Mary, and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true, and that Hell is true, May God admit him to Paradise for what he was doing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10620","I am Yusuf bin Hammad, from Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: “The last verse that was revealed was: They ask you for a question.” Say, “May God give you a fatwa regarding the calamity.”"
"10621","I am Muhammad bin Mansour, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, saying: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: “I fell ill, so he came to me.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, were returning to me as they were walking, and they found that I had fainted, so he performed ablution. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he poured his ablution on me and I woke up. I said: O Messenger of God, how do I make a will about my money? How do I make a will about my money? How do I do with it? What about it? He did not answer me at all, until the verse of inheritance was revealed: They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “May God give you a fatwa regarding the calamity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10622","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Maadan bin Abi Talha Al-Yamari, that Omar bin Al-Khattab delivered a sermon on Friday, and said: I will not leave anything after me more important to me than kalaala, nor will he be harsh with me in anything. Ever since, meaning his company, he had never been harsh to me in his callousness, until he stabbed his finger in my chest and said: “O Umar, the sign of summer that is in Surah An-Nisa, “And indeed, if I live, I will judge in it a matter with which those who read the Qur’an and those who do not read will be judged.” . . Brief"
"10623","I am Ali bin Hajar, Sa’dan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Subaie, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “The last verses “The last Surah An-Nisa was revealed in the Qur’an.”"
"10624","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abdullah bin Idris, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: A Jew said For Omar, if this verse had been revealed to us, the Jews, we would have taken it as a holiday: “Today I have perfected for you your religion.” Omar said: “Today I have learned On which it was revealed, and the night on which it was revealed, Friday night, and we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat.”"
"10625","I am Ishaq bin Mansour, I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, he said: I entered upon Aisha, she said to me: Do you read Surat Al-Ma’idah? I said: Yes, she said: “But it is the last surah to be revealed, so whatever you find in it of what is permissible, make it lawful, and whatever you find in it of what is forbidden, make it forbidden.” He asked her about the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: The Qur’an."
"10626","I am Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hassan. He said: My father is me, on the authority of Al-Hussein, on the authority of Yazid, L 8369. I am Muhammad bin Aqeel, I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, my father told me, Yazid the grammarian told me, Ikrimah told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Who He disbelieved in stoning, so he disbelieved in the Qur’an in a way he did not expect, and that is the saying of God Almighty: O People of the Book, our Messenger has come to you explaining \You will have much of what you concealed from the Book"
"10627","I am Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Nadr. He said: Abu al-Nadr, narrated to me Ubayd Allah al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharriq, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Al-Miqdad came on the day of Badr while he was riding a horse of his, and he said: O Messenger of God, we do not say as the Banu Israel to Moses: So go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are sitting here. But go ahead, and we are with you. It is as if he had been kept secret. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"10628","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Khaled, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked to Badr, So he consulted the Muslims, and Abu Bakr advised him, then he consulted a man, and Omar advised him, then he consulted them, and the Ansar said: Oh Community of Ansar, beware of you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wants to say: Then we will not say as the Children of Israel said to Moses: So go you. And your Lord, so fight. Here we sit. By the One who has sent you with the truth, if you had gone to Burk al-Ghimād, we would have followed you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10629","I am Ali bin Khashram, I am Issa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “No soul is killed unjustly except that a measure of its blood is due from the first son of Adam, because he was the first to institute killing.”"
"10630","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas: “A group of They came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they converted to Islam and went to Medina. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to bring camels. charity, and they drank from its urine and milk, so they killed its shepherd and drank it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a caravan in search of them. So they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet, and gouged out their eyes, but did not remove them from their bodies, and left them until they died, and God Almighty sent down “The recompense is only for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10631","I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala, narrated by Abu Muawiyah, narrated by Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: He passed by the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, a flogged, bathed Jew. He called them and said: “Do you find the punishment for the adulterer in your book?” They said: Yes, so he called a man from... Their scholars, so he said: “I adjure you by God who sent down the Torah to Moses. Is this how you find the punishment for the adulterer in your book?” So he said: No, and had it not been You asked me, but I did not tell you. We find that the punishment for the adulterer in our book is stoning, but he appeared among our nobles, so if we took the honorable man, we would leave him. And when we take a weak man and impose punishment on him, we say: Let us come together on something that we will impose on the honorable and the lowly, so we agreed to be careful. And flogging, and we abandoned stoning, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was the first to revive your cause when they killed him, so he ordered that he be stoned.” So God Almighty revealed: O Messenger, let not those who hasten into disbelief grieve you: And if you do not give it, beware. He says: Go Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, if he gives you a fatwa regarding bathing and flogging, then take him, and if he gives you a fatwa of stoning, then beware, to his saying: And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed - those are the disbelievers, in the Jews, and to his saying: And whoever does not rule by what God has revealed Those are the wrongdoers, according to the Jews, until His saying: And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed, those are the transgressors. He said: Among the disbelievers. All of them mean the verse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10632","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, from Khalid, from Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Al-Rabi’ al-Thaniya broke the jaw of a running girl, so they asked for forgiveness, but they refused. So they offered them injuries, but they refused. They came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered retaliation. Anas bin al-Nadr said: O Messenger of God, The spring bend is broken? By the One who sent you with the truth, do not break it. He said: “O Anas, the Book of God is retaliation.” The people were satisfied and pardoned, and he said: “Indeed, among the servants of God are those who “I swear on God that I will fulfill it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10633","I am Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who “If he gives something in charity from his body, God will atone for him an amount of his sins.”"
"10634","Ibrahim bin Ya’qub told me, on the authority of Ja’far bin Aoun, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Three: Whoever says one of them, then the greatest lie against God is: He who claims that he knows what is in the morrow, and God says: No soul knows what it will gain tomorrow, and whoever claims that Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, concealed any of the revelation, and God says: O The Messenger: Convey what has been sent down to you from your Lord, and if you do not do so, then you have not conveyed his message. And whoever claims that Muhammad saw his Lord has magnified God’s will. Lies, and God says: Sights do not overtake Him, but He overtakes sights, and He is the Gentle, the All-Aware. And it is not possible for a human being to speak to him except God. By revelation or from behind a veil, so I said: O Mother of the Believers, did he not say: And He saw it at another revelation, and He saw it on the clear horizon? She said: We asked the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said: “I saw Gabriel descending from the horizon on his appearance and appearance, or on His creation and His image prevail over what is between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10635","I am Amr bin Ali, this is Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam, he said: I heard Hisham bin Urwa speaking, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, He said: “This verse was revealed about Al-Najashi and his companions: And when they hear what was revealed to the Messenger, you will see their eyes overflowing with tears.”"
"10636","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, regarding his saying: “May God not punish you.” “By the idle talk of your oaths.” She said: “It was revealed about a man saying: ‘No, by God.’ Yes, by God.”"
"10637","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Jarir, and Waki’, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: “We used to fight with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there were no women with us. So we said: O Messenger of God, should we not castrate? He forbade us from that, and permitted us to do so. We marry the woman with the garment for a certain period of time. Then he recited: “O you who have believed, do not prohibit the good things that God has made lawful for you.”"
"10638","I am Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim Sa’iqa, I am Hajjaj bin Minhal, we are Rabi’a bin Kulthum bin Jabr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The prohibition of alcohol was revealed in two of the Ansar tribes. They drank to the point that when they were drunk, they disturbed each other. When they woke up, the man saw the mark on his face, head, and beard, and said: My brother has done this to me, and they were brothers who had nothing in their hearts. Grudges. By God, if my Lord had been compassionate and merciful, he would not have done this to me. Grudges fell into their hearts, so God Almighty revealed: Alcohol and gambling, to his saying: Have you abstained from it? Then some people said: It is an abomination, and it is in the stomach of so-and-so who was killed on the day of Badr, and so-and-so was killed. On the day of Uhud, then God Almighty revealed: There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have been fed with, as long as they fear God and believe and do righteous deeds. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10639","Qutayba bin Saeed narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The one with two stalks from Abyssinia will destroy the Kaaba.”"
"10640","I am Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Khalid bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abd God, He said: When it was revealed: “There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have been fed with, as long as they feared and believed and did righteous deeds and then feared. And they believed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is one of them."
"10641","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, Al-Nadr narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Anas, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conveyed the message He (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said something about his companions, so he delivered a sermon and said: “Paradise and Hell were presented to me, and I have never seen anything like today in good and evil, and if only you knew.” I do not know that you laughed little and wept much.” He said: No day has come to the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a day more severe than this. He said: They covered their heads, and they had two buttocks, so Omar bin Al-Khattab stood up and said: O Messenger of God, we are satisfied with God as our Lord and with Islam as our religion. And Muhammad is a prophet. Then that man got up and said: Who is my father? He said: “Your father is so-and-so.” He said: Then it was revealed: “O you who have believed, do not ask about things that, if they are made known to you, will harm you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10642","I am Mujahid bin Musa, from Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of his father, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he looked at me and straightened it, and said: “Do I want camels or sheep?” I said: Of all of them, God has given me more and more, and He said: “Aren’t you It produces its eyes and ears, so this one opens and says: Lake, and this one gapes? \one\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"10643","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, narrated by Yaqoub, narrated by Abi, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ibn Al-Musayyab said, Abu said Huraira: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw Amr bin Luhayy al-Khuza’i dragging his reed through the fire, and he was the first to let his swords burn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10644","I am Utbah bin Abdullah, I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, I am Ismail, on the authority of Qais, he said: I heard Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq saying: O People, you are reading this verse: “O you who have believed! You have your own souls. He who goes astray will not harm you if you are guided. Indeed, I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “If a people sees an evil and does not change it, God will punish them with punishment.”"
"10645","I am Imran bin Yazid, we are Marwan, we are Othman bin Hakim, Saeed bin Yassar told me that Ibn Abbas told him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, he used to recite in the two rak’ahs of Fajr, in the first of which was the verse to his saying: We believe in God and what has been revealed to us, etc. verse, and in the other: “We believe and bear witness that we are Muslims.”"
"10646","I am Al-Qasim bin Zakaria, from Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, and Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Who brings us the news of the people?” Al-Zubayr said: “I do.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed “Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10647","I am Muhammad bin Bashar. Ishaq bin Yusuf, my name is Sufyan, told me. And I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up among the people and admonished them, and said: “O people, you will be gathered together before God, barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” Then He recited: Just as We initiated the first creation, We will return it as a promise upon Us: Indeed, we will do it. Then men will be brought from my nation, and they will be taken to the north, so I say: O Lord, my nation is my nation. Then it will be said: Do you know what they did after you? So I will say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I remained among them. To: The Mighty, the Wise, and it will be said: They have not ceased to be apostates ever since I separated from them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10648","I am Nuh bin Habib, we are Yahya, meaning bin Saeed, we are Qudamah bin Abdullah, Jasra bint Dajjah narrated to me, she said: I heard Abu Dhar, saying: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose until morning with a sign, and the verse is: If you punish them, they are your servants, and if you forgive them, For you are the Mighty, the Wise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10649","On the authority of Zakaria bin Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Jesus, peace be upon him, received his proof, God met him when he said: And when God said, “O Jesus, son of Mary, did you say to the people, ‘Take me and my mother as two gods besides God?’” Abu Huraira: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Then God met him and said: Glory be to You, it is not for me to say,” the entire verse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10650","Muhammad ibn Bashar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, informed us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’d, in this verse: “ And do not expel those who call on their Lord in the morning and the evening. He said: It was revealed about six: I, and Ibn Masoud among them, so it was revealed that the call to prayer \For these\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"10651","I am Muhammad bin Al-Nadr, Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, and Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: When it was revealed: “Say, ‘He is capable of sending down upon you a torment from above you.’ The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I seek refuge in Your Face.” He said: Or from under your feet, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I seek refuge in Your Face.” Or he will cover you with sects, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: “This is easier.” The wording is from Qutaybah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10652","I am Muhammad Ibn Rafi’, I am Abd al-Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir, he said: When it was revealed: “Say, He is the Powerful.” On the condition that He sends upon you a torment from above you. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I seek refuge in your face,” or from under your feet. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I seek refuge in Your Face,” or He will separate you into sects. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is easier.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Some of the letters of “U Yalbakum” were not authentically transmitted from Muhammad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10653","I am Bishr ibn Khalid, I am Muhammad ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “When This verse was revealed: “Those who believe and do not mix their faith with injustice. The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Which of us has not been wronged? ? Then God Almighty revealed: Indeed, polytheism is a great injustice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10654","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, from Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ No one should say: I am better than Yunus bin Matthew. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10655","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym al-Zarqi, said: Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi told me that they said: O Messenger of God, how can we pray for you? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and his wives and his descendants, as You sent blessings upon the family of Abraham, and bless upon Muhammad and his wives and his descendants, just as You blessed the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10656","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saad, on the authority of my uncle, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that he prostrated in the Prophet, then He said: The Prophet of God was commanded that I follow the prophets, then he read: Those are the ones whom God has guided, so follow their guidance. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10657","I am Utba bin Abdullah, I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrating In: p.: Those are the ones whom God has guided, so follow their guidance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10658","I am Amr bin Ali, from Yahya, from Sufyan. Harun bin Abi Waki’ told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the words of the Almighty: “And do not eat of that on which the name of God has not been mentioned.” He said: The polytheists disputed with them and said: “Whatever God has slaughtered, do not eat it, and whatever you have slaughtered.” Did you eat it?"
"10659","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It reached Omar that Samurah sold wine, so he said: God killed Samura. Did he not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God killed the Jews. Fat was forbidden to them, so they made it beautiful.” He said Sufyan: meaning they melted it"
"10660","I am Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Bashhar, they said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far, i.e. Shu`bah, narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Wael, he said: I heard Abdullah, saying: And he raised it, saying: “No one, meaning, is more jealous than God, and for that reason He forbade immoral acts, both apparent and belly, and no one loves praise more than God Almighty, and for that reason he praised himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10661","I am Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, from Hammad, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter for us. One day he handed over a line, and Asim wrote it out for us, saying: “This is the way of God.” Then he wrote lines to the right of the line and to the left of it, and said: These paths, and these paths, on each path there is a devil calling to it. Then he recited this verse: And this is My path, straight, so follow it. For the first path, and do not follow the paths, for the path, for He diverted you from His path; that is He enjoined upon you that you may become righteous."
"10662","I am Al-Fadl Ibn Al-Abbas Ibn Ibrahim, I am Ahmad Ibn Yunus, I am Abu Bakr, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger wrote God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a line, and he wrote lines to the right of the line and to the left of it, then he said: This is the path of God, straight, and these paths are on “Every path thereof is a devil calling to it.” Then he recited: “And indeed, this is My path, straight.”"
"10663","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you know where this sun is going?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “For it is running.” Until it reaches its resting place under the throne, and it is said to it: Rise and rise from the west, and it will rise from the west.” The Messenger said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you know what that is? That is when: no soul will benefit from its belief if it did not believe before.”"
"10664","I am Ahmad bin Harb, narrated by Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “The Hour will not come until the sun rises from the west. If it rises and the people see it, those who are on it will be safe. That is when: it will not benefit a soul.” She had never believed before.” And on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Ghaylan, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amara ibn al-Qaqa’, with it"
"10665","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawir narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zurr, who said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, and said: Have you learned from the Messenger of God? Did God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, have a conversation about his desires? He said: Yes, we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. He named him Asim, when a man who was in the company of the people called him in a voice. He had a harsh voice and said: O Muhammad, O Muhammad. So the people said to him: “Mh, you have been forbidden from doing this.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, answered him in a voice similar to that: “Haoum.” “Haoum,” and he said: The man loves people, and why does he follow them? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A person is with the one he loves,” and he continued to talk to us until he told us: “Indeed, God has made Morocco a gate.” The journey of its exposure is seventy years for repentance, and it will not be closed unless the sun rises before it.” He said: “That is what God Almighty says: The day “Some of the signs of your Lord will come; the belief of which will not benefit a soul if it had not believed before or earned any good in its belief.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10666","I am Ali bin Khashram, I am Issa, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He repented before the sun rose from the west, may God accept his repentance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10667","I am Abu Salih al-Makki, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, extends His hand to the sinner of the night so that he may repent by day, and to the sinner of the day to repent by night, until “The sun rises from the west.”"
"10668","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “God said God Almighty: If My servant intends to do a good deed, write it down for him, and if he does it, write it down ten times as much, and if he intends to do an evil deed, then do not You write it down. If he does it, write it as one, and if he leaves it, write it as good.”"
"10669","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Salamah, he said: I heard Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “A woman used to go around the Kaaba while she was naked, and she would say: Today some or all of it is visible, and whatever is visible of it I will not make lawful.” So she came down: O children of Adam, take your adornment to every mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10670","I am Muhammad bin Adam bin Suleiman, and Muhammad bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “No one is more jealous than God, and for this reason He has forbidden immoral acts, whether apparent or hidden, and there is no one more beloved to Him than praise.” From God,” the wording is from Ibn Al-Ala (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10671","I am Muhammad bin Idris, from Ubaid bin Yaish, from Yahya bin Adam, from Hamza bin Habib, from Abu Ishaq, from Al-Aghar, from my father Hurairah, and Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “And we wish that you would be blessed with Paradise.” He said: “We wish that you may be healthy and not fall ill, and be blessed and not fall ill.” “Have a miserable life, grow young, and do not grow old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10672","I am Muhammad ibn Rafi’, Abd al-Razzaq told us, I am Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Waqid al-Laythi, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Hunayn, and we passed by Sidra. I said: O Messenger of God, make this a destination for us. Anawaat, just as the infidels have anawaat, and the infidels used to attach their weapons to a sidra and gather around it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: “Allah is the Greatest. This is as the Children of Israel said: Make for us a god as they have gods. Indeed, you are following the traditions of those who \before you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"10673","I am Humayd bin Masada, from Bishr, from Dawud, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Moses met Adam.” Peace be upon them both. He said: Are you Adam, the father of humanity, who made people miserable and drove them out? He said: Yes. He said: Are you not Moses whom God chose? With his message and his words? He said: Yes. He said: Do you not find in what God has revealed to you that He will take me out of it before He enters it? He said: Yes Then Adam disputed with Moses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10674","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he greeted: “Moses said to Adam: Are you the one who disappointed the people and expelled them from Paradise? Then Adam said: You are the one whom God chose and wrote for you with His own hand.” Torah, do you blame me for something that God decreed for me forty years before he created me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10675","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am An-Nadr, I am Shu’bah, I am Abd al-Malik bin Umair. He said: I heard Amr bin Harith, saying: I heard Saeed bin Zaid. Ibn Amr Ibn Nufayl, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.” I am Muhammad. Ibn Al-Muthanna, and Amr Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shu’bah, Al-Hakam told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Urni, on the authority of Amr Ibn Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Shu'bah said: When Al-Hakam told me about it, I did not deny it from the hadith of Abdul-Malik. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10676","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar Al-Juhani said that Omar bin Al-Khattab was asked about this verse: And when your Lord took from the children of Adam from their backs their offspring. And they testified against themselves. Am I not your Lord? They said, “Yes, we testified,” lest you say on the Day of Resurrection, “Indeed, we were unaware of this.” Then Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, being asked about her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty created Adam and wiped His back with his right hand, and He extracted from him offspring, and said: I created these for Paradise, and for the deeds of the people of Paradise they will do. Then he wiped his back. So He produced offspring from him, and said: I created these for the Fire, and they will do the work of the people of the Fire. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, so what is the work? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God Almighty creates a servant for Paradise, He uses him to do the work of the people of Paradise until he dies on the verge of Paradise.” The work of the people of Paradise, so God will admit him to Paradise, and if the servant is created for Hell, He will use him to do the work of the people of Hell until he dies doing the work of the people of Hell. And He will cause him to enter the Fire therewith.”"
"10677","I am Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim, I am Al-Hussein bin Muhammad, I am Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Kulthum bin Jabr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God, Blessed and Most High, took the covenant from the back of Adam through Numan, meaning Arafat, and brought From his loins every offspring that he produced, and he scattered them before his hands like atoms, then he spoke to them slowly, saying: Am I not your Lord? They said, “Yes, we bear witness that You will say on the Day of Resurrection, ‘Indeed, we were heedless of this.’” Until the end of the verse, Al-Nasa’i said: This Kulthum is not strong, and his hadith is not With the preserved (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10678","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, neither Khaled, nor Shu’bah. Ya’la bin Ata informed me, saying: I heard Nafi’ bin Asim, saying: Abd said: God: His saying: “We gave him Our signs, and he separated from them. He said: They were revealed about Umayyah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10679","I am Humaid bin Masada, we are Bishr, meaning bin Al-Mufaddal, I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, in His saying: “And recite to them the story of the one to whom We gave Our signs, and he separated from them. He said: It was Balam, and he said: It was revealed in Umayyad.”"
"10680","I am Amr bin Ali, from Abdul Rahman, from Saeed bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ghaytif bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Yaqoub, and Nafi’ Ibn Asim, on the authority of Abdul Allah bin Amr: In this verse: We gave him Our signs, and he separated from them. He said: He is Umayyah bin Abi Al-Salt."
"10681","I am Harun bin Ishaq, narrated by Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr. He said: “God, Blessed and Most High, only revealed: Take forgiveness from people’s morals.”"
"10682","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: I came on the day of Badr with a sword to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: God has healed my chest today from the enemy, so he gave me this sword. He said: This sword “It is neither mine nor yours.” So I went, saying: He will be given today who has not afflicted me. While I was there, the Messenger came to me and said: Answer, so I thought. Something was revealed about my words, so I came and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You asked me for this sword, and it is not mine nor yours, and God He made it for me, and it is for you. Then he recited: They ask you about the Anfal. Say: The Anfal belongs to God and the Messenger, until the end of the verse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10683","I am Al-Haytham bin Ayyub, we are Al-Mu`tamir bin Suleiman, he said: I heard Dawud bin Abi Hind speaking, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever goes to such-and-such a place, or does such-and-such, will have such-and-such,” so he hastened to him. The young men, and the old men stood firm under the banners, and when God granted them victory, the young men came asking for what had been given to them, but the old men said: Do not go with him. Rather than us, we were only a response to you, so God Almighty revealed: So fear God and make peace between you."
"10684","I am Amr bin Ali, I am Abdul Rahman, I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: “I raised my head on the day of Uhud Then I did not see any of the people except that he was slumbering under his cover.”"
"10685","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, who said: “I was among those upon whom drowsiness descended on the Day of Resurrection. Uhud, until my sword fell from my hand repeatedly.”"
"10686","I am Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, I am Hassan bin Abdullah, I am Khallad bin Sulaiman, Nafi’ told me that he asked Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I said: We are a people who do not stand firm when fighting our enemy, and we do not know who the group is? He said to me: “The category is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” So I said: God says in His Book: O you who have believed, when you meet those who disbelieve Marching forth, so do not turn your backs to them. He said: This was only revealed to the people of Badr, neither before it nor after it."
"10687","I am Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad. My uncle told us, my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah bin told me. Tha'labah bin Su'air said: “The one who opened the battle on the day of Badr was Abu Jahl, and he said when the people met: Oh God, which of us is more decisive? To the womb, and it came for what we do not know, so tomorrow will be opened, and that was its opening, so God revealed: If you open, then the opening has come to you.”"
"10688","I am Bishr bin Khalid, I am Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, and Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Abdullah said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that the Quraysh had disobeyed, he said: “Oh God, help me with seven like the seventh of Joseph.” So the Sunnah took hold of them until It harvested everything until they ate the skins and it made it come out of the ground like smoke, so Abu Sufyan came to him and said: Oh Muhammad, your people have They perished, so pray to God to reveal them. So he called and said: “If they return, we will return.” This is in the hadith of Mansour, then he recited this verse: So wait for the day when the sky brings forth clear smoke. He said: The torment of the Hereafter. The smoke, the oppression, and the obligation have passed. One of them said: The moon, and the other said: And the Romans. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10689","I am Abu Dawud. He said: I am Abu Zayd al-Harawi, from Shu`bah, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa`id: “And who He will turn his back to them on that day. He said: It was revealed about the people of Badr."
"10690","I am Humayd bin Masada, on the authority of Bishr, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: “It was revealed on the day of Badr: And who That Day He will turn His back to them.”"
"10691","I am Imran bin Musa, from Yazid, from Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He came out The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Ubayy ibn Ka’b while he was praying. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Oh, my father.” Then my father turned. He did not answer him, then my father prayed and made it easy, then he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: “Woe to you, what prevented my father from answering my invitation when I called you?” He said: O Messenger of God, I was in prayer. He said: “You will not find anything in what God has revealed.” Until: “Respond to God and to the Messenger when he calls you to revive you.” He said: “Yes, O Messenger of God, I will not return, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted him and said: “Would you like me to teach you a Surah like it that was not revealed in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Qur’an?” He said: Yes. That is, the Messenger of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I hope that you will not leave this door until you know it.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took He held my hand and spoke to me, and I was slowing down for fear that she would reach the door before the conversation ended. When we approached the door, I said: Oh Messenger of God, what is the surah that you promised me? He said: “How do you recite during prayer?” So I recited to him the Mother of the Qur’an. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, what was revealed in “The Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Criterion like it, for it is the Seven Repeated Verses and the Great Qur’an which I have been given.”"
"10692","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, I am Jarir bin Hazim, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, he said: “When This verse was revealed: And beware of a trial that will not strike those of you who have done wrong, especially the verse. He said: And we will be present on that day. He said: So I made Do you wonder at this verse: What temptation will afflict us? What is this temptation that we have not seen it?"
"10693","I am Abdah bin Abdullah, I am Suwayd, on the authority of Zuhayr, we have a statement, that Wabarah, Sa`id bin Jubayr narrated to him that a man, said to Abdullah Ibn Omar: O Abu Abdul Rahman, what do you think of fighting during sedition? He said: Do you know what temptation is? “May your mother be bereaved of you. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to fight the polytheists, and entering into them was a temptation, and your fighting is only for the sake of kingship.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10694","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, our father is Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God fed us the spoils out of mercy and out of mercy for us, and He made light of us because He knew of our weakness.”"
"10695","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, from Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The spoils were not permissible for a black-headed people before you. Fire used to come down from the sky and consume it. So when the Day of At Badr, people hurried with the spoils, so God Almighty revealed: “If it had not been a decree from God that had preceded,” until the end of the verse: “So eat of what you have spoiled lawfully.” “Good” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10696","Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulaiman told me, on the authority of Hafs, who is Ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, who said: Abu Ishaq included me in him. He said: Indeed, I love you for the sake of God. Abu Al-Ahwas told me, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “When this verse was revealed: If you spend what is in The earth has not united their hearts together. He said: They are those who love one another for the sake of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10697","I am Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Abdullah bin Salem told us, Ali bin Abi Talha told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, In the Almighty’s saying: “Had it not been for a Book from God that had preceded, a great torment would have affected you while you took it.” He said: “Mercy from God has preceded for them.” to commit sin.”"
"10698","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, I am Muhammad, na Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Bara’, saying: “The last verse to be revealed: the verse of Kalaala, and the last Surah revealed: Bara’ah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10699","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Garqada, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, during the Farewell Pilgrimage, he said: “O people, three times, what day is this?” They said: The Day of Sacrifice, the greatest day of Hajj. He said: “Your blood, your property, and your honor are sacred among you, just as this day of yours is sacred. Should a criminal not commit a crime against his child, nor He was born after his father. Indeed, Satan has longed to be worshiped in this country of yours forever, but he will be obedient to him in some of the things you despise. of your deeds and he will be satisfied. Verily, all usury of ignorance is forgiven. Yours is yours. You shall not wrong or be wronged. You shall not be wronged. Verily, every blood Some of the blood of the pre-Islamic period is shed, and the first of it that I shed is the blood of Al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib. He was breast-feeding among the Banu Layth, so I killed him. Hudhayl, “O my mothers, have I conveyed the message?” three times. They said: “Yes.” He said: “O God, bear witness.”"
"10700","I am Muhammad ibn Bashar. Muhammad and Uthman ibn Umar narrated to me, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Muharrar ibn Abi Huraira, on the authority of his father, said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to the people of Mecca in a clearing. He said: What were you calling? He said: We used to proclaim: “No one will enter Paradise except a believing soul, and no naked person will circumambulate the Kaaba, and whoever is between him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Upon him, peace and blessings be upon him, he made a covenant, and he fixed it and extended it to four months. When the four months have passed, then God is free from the polytheists. And His Messenger, and no polytheist will perform Hajj after the year.” And I was calling until my voice became clear. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10701","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, and he was turning His hand, he said: “There are only four of the hypocrites remaining. One of them is very old today. If he drank cold water, he would not feel cold.”"
"10702","I am Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid, we are Ali bin Ayyash, we are Shuaib, Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what Abdul Rahman Al-Araj told him, from what he mentioned He heard Abu Hurairah talking about it. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The treasure of one of them on the Day of Resurrection will be the brave one, the one who bald his head. Its owner flees from him, and asks him: I am your treasure, and he does not continue with it until his finger touches it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10703","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The treasure of one of you on the Day of Resurrection will be a brave man with two raisins, one who follows his companion while he seeks refuge.” And he continues to follow it until his finger touches it.”"
"10704","I am Abu Salih al-Makki, from Fudayl, meaning ibn Iyad, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: I came to al-Rabdha and entered upon Abu Dharr. So I said: What has brought you this? He said: I was in the Levant, and I read this verse: “And those who hoard up gold and silver but do not spend them,” until the end of the verse, so Muawiyah said: “This verse was not revealed about us, rather it was about the People of the Book,” so I said: “It is about us and about the People of the Book,” until it was said There was a dispute, and he wrote to Uthman complaining about me. Uthman, may God have mercy on him, wrote to me to come, so I went to the city, and the people gathered behind me as if they were They never saw me, so I entered upon Othman, and I complained to him about this, and he said: Step aside, and be close. So I stayed at this place, and by God, if an Ethiopian were to rule over me, I would not disobey him, nor would I go back on what I said.”"
"10705","Nasr bin Ali narrated to us, Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, Salama bin Nabit said, I am Nuaym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Nabit bin Shait, on the authority of Salim bin Ubaid: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, the Ansar said: Among us is a leader and from you is a leader. Then Umar said: “Who has someone like These three? When they were in the cave, who were they? When he said to his companion, “Do not be sad, God is with us.” Who were they? He extended his hand, and the people pledged allegiance to him with a good and beautiful pledge.”"
"10706","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, our name is Muhammad, meaning Ibn Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was swearing an oath, Ibn Abi Al-Khuwaysarah Al-Tamimi came and said: Be fair. O Messenger of God, he said: “Woe to you, who will do justice if I do not do justice?” Then Omar said: O Messenger of God, give me permission to behead him. He said: Leave him, for he has companions whose prayers one of you deems to be in contempt with his prayers, and his fasting with his fasting. They pass away from the debt as an arrow passes from the target. Then he looks at its dirt, but nothing is found in it. Then one looks at its freshness, but nothing is found in it. Then one looks at its surface, and nothing is found in it. Then He looks at his chest and nothing is found in it, above all dung and blood. I mean, a man with black hair on one hand, or one of his hands like a breast. A woman, or something like a group of people, will come out from time to time.” He said: So it was revealed about them: “And among them are those who will touch you in Alms.” Abu Sa’id said: I bear witness that I heard this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I bear witness that when Ali killed them, he came A man according to the description that was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10707","I am Hanad bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said Ali, peace be upon him, while he was in Yemen, sent some gold to present to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he divided it among four: Al-Aqra' bin Habis Al-Hanathili, Uyaynah bin Badr Al-Fazari, Alqamah bin Ulathah Al-Amiri, then one of the Banu Kilab, Zayd Al-Ta'i, then One of the Banu Nabhan. The Quraysh became angry, and he said again: “The saddles of Quraysh,” so they said: Will he give the saddles of Najd and leave us? ! He said: “I only did that to get along with them.” Then a man with a thick beard, with high cheeks, sunken eyes, and a prominent forehead came, He had a shaved head, so he said: Fear God, O Muhammad. He said: “Who will obey God if I disobey Him? He will trust me over the people of the earth, and you will not trust me?” He said: The man planned, and a man from among the people asked permission to kill him. They believed that he was Khalid bin Al-Walid, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” Indeed, from the light of this are people who recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats. They kill the people of Islam and call upon the people of idols. They will pass away from Islam just as an arrow passes away from a target. If I overtake them, I will kill them with the same method of killing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10708","I am Ubaidullah bin Saad bin Ibrahim, from my uncle, from my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Anas bin Malik told me that he said: When God repaid His Messenger what he repaid in terms of wealth. They say on the day of Hunayn: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to give men from the Quraysh a hundred of Camels, then a man from the Ansar said: May God forgive the Messenger of God if he gives to men from Quraysh and leaves us, while our swords are dripping with their blood? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will give men a message about their covenant of disbelief, so I will talk to them. Would you not be satisfied that the people should go? With the money and you return to your camps with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, it is better for what you return to, it is better than what they return with.” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, we are satisfied."
"10709","I am Bishr bin Khalid, from Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us May God bless him and grant him peace, with charity. Abu Aqeel gave half a saa’ in charity, and a person brought something more than him, so the hypocrites said: Indeed, God is All-Sufficient. About the charity of this man, and this other did nothing but hypocrisy, so it was revealed: \their effort\"""""""
"10710","I am Amr bin Ali, na Yahya, na Ubaid Allah. Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: When Abdullah bin Abi died, he came His son went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Give me your shirt so that I may shroud him, pray for him, and ask forgiveness for him. So he gave him his shirt, then He said: “If you have finished, then permit me to pray for him.” Then Omar pulled him away and said: Has God forbid you to pray for hypocrites? He said: “I am between two choices. He said: Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them.” So he prayed for him, so God Almighty revealed: And do not pray for him. One of them has never died, and you cannot stand over his grave, so he left off praying for them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10711","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, they said: Hujain bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God have mercy on him, he said: When Abdullah bin Abi bin Salul died. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was called for him to pray over him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose I jumped to him and then said: O Messenger of God, will you pray for my father’s son? On the day of such-and-such he said: such-and-such. I will repeat his statement over him. ? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled, or said: “Give it up for me, O Umar.” When I insisted on him, he said: “I was given a choice, so I chose. I know that if I add more than seventy, he will be forgiven for adding more than that. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over him, and he only stayed for a little while until... The two verses were revealed from Bara’ah: “And do not pray for any of them ever who dies.” I was astonished at my audacity against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, by God. And His Messenger knows best (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10712","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, from Yahya, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Muhammad bin Jafar, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Awf, from Abu Raja, from Samra. Ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to his companions: “Has any of you seen a vision?” So he would narrate whoever he wanted to. He tells the story, and that one day he said to us: “Two men came to me tonight, and they sent me away, and they said to me: Go, and I went with them.” So we arrived at a city built of bricks of gold and silver. We came to the gate of the city. We opened and it was opened for us. We entered and they met us. There are men with a half of their creation like the best of what you are seeing, and a half like the ugliest of what you are seeing. So he said to them: Go, and they fell into that. The river, and behold, it was wide and flowing, as if its water was pure white. So they went and fell into it, then returned to us. That had disappeared. The evil came from them, and they became like the best form, so they said to me: This is the Garden of Eden, and this is your abode. As I looked up, I saw it shortened, they said. To me: This is your home. I said to them: May God bless you both. Let me enter it. They said: As for now, no, and you are inside it. He said: The people who were Half of them were good, and half of them were bad, for they mixed a good deed with another bad deed, so God forgave them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10713","I am Suwaid bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu al-Hubab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no believer who gives in charity from good earnings, and God does not accept anything except that which is good, except God. He takes it from him with his right hand and grows it as one of you nurtures his foal or his offspring, until the fruit reaches the size of a man.”"
"10714","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Al-Layth, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Ibn Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that He said: Two men debated in the mosque that was founded on piety from the first day. One man said: It is the Quba Mosque, and the other said: It is a mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is my mosque.”"
"10715","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, from Ibn Abi Omar, from Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd, on the authority of his father, he said: “ “The mosque that was founded on piety is the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"10716","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Our name is Muhammad, meaning Ibn Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, he said When Abu Talib was about to die, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon him, and with him were: Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah, and he said: “I.e. Uncle, say: There is no god but God, a word for which I will plead with you with God.” Then Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah said to him: O Abu Talib, Do you renounce the religion of Abdul Muttalib? They continued speaking to him until he said the last thing he spoke to them: following the religion of Abdul Mutallib. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will ask forgiveness for you.” Unless I forbid you.” Then it was revealed: “It is not for the Prophet and those who have believed to ask forgiveness for the polytheists,” and it was revealed: “Indeed, you do not guide whom you love.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10717","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Al-Makhzoumi, Mahdi bin Maymun told me, on the authority of Ghailan bin Jarir, he said: I said to Anas: “Have you seen Community of Ansar, is this the name by which you were called, or did God, Blessed and Most High, name you? He said: Rather, God named us by it?"
"10718","Yusuf ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us — Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us — 'Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me that 'Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik — who had been the guide of Ka'b among his sons when he lost his sight — said: ""I heard Ka'b ibn Malik narrating his account when he stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, during the expedition of Tabuk. He said: 'While I was sitting in that state which Allah has mentioned of us — my soul had become constricted upon me, and the earth had become constricted upon me despite its vastness — I heard a caller calling out from upon a mountain with the loudest voice: O Ka'b ibn Malik, receive glad tidings! I fell prostrating, and I knew that relief had come. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, announced Allah's acceptance of our repentance when he prayed the Fajr prayer. The people came rushing to give us glad tidings. People went to my two companions with glad tidings. A man galloped a horse toward me, and a runner from Aslam hastened to a mountain. The voice was swifter than the horse. When the one whose voice I had heard came to me, he gave me glad tidings. I took off my two garments and gave them to them both as a token of joy — by Allah, I owned nothing else — and I borrowed two garments and put them on. I set out toward the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. The people met me in groups, congratulating me on the repentance, saying: May Allah's repentance bring you joy! Ka'b said: Until I entered the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, sitting with the people around him. Talha ibn 'Ubayd Allah came hastening toward me until he shook my hand and congratulated me. By Allah, no man from the Muhajirun stood up for me other than him, and I shall never forget that for Talha. Ka'b said: When I gave the salam to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, he said — and his face was beaming with joy: Receive the glad tidings of the best day that has come upon you since your mother gave birth to you. I said: From you, O Messenger of Allah, or from Allah? He said: No, rather from Allah. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he was joyful, his face would shine as if it were a piece of the moon, and we used to recognize that in him. When I sat before him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed, part of my repentance is that I divest myself of my wealth as a charity to Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, and to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: Hold on to some of your wealth, for that is better for you. I said: Then I shall hold on to my share that is in Khaybar. I said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed, Allah the Exalted only saved me through truthfulness, and indeed, part of my repentance is that I shall not speak except the truth for as long as I remain. By Allah, no Muslim has Allah tested in truthfulness of speech since I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, better than He has tested me. And you do not know — since I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace — any lie from me. And I hope that Allah will protect me in what remains. Then Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed: Allah has turned in repentance to the Prophet, and the Muhajirun, and the Ansar who followed him in the hour of difficulty — reciting until: the truthful ones. By Allah, Allah has not blessed me with any blessing after He guided me to Islam that is greater in my soul than the truthfulness of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, on that day — that I did not lie to him and perish as those who lied to him perished — until the revelation came down with the worst of what He said to anyone: They will swear by Allah to you when you return to them, that you may turn away from them — until: the transgressors. Ka'b said: And we three were left behind from the affair of those from whom the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, accepted when they swore to him. He pledged allegiance to them and sought forgiveness for them. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, deferred our affair until Allah decided it. For that reason, Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, said: And upon the three who were left behind. That which Allah mentions is not about staying behind from the expedition; rather, it is His deferring us and His postponing our affair from those who swore to him and offered excuses to him and from whom He accepted."""
"10719","I am Ali bin Hajar, and Amr bin Othman bin Saeed, they said: We are Baqiyya, and he is Ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Al-Nawwas bin Sam’an, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has set forth as an example a path Straight on both shoulders of the path are two walls with open doors, and on the doors is a wall. A caller calls at the head of the path, and a caller calls from above it. And God invites to the abode of peace and guides whom He wills to a straight path. The gates on the shoulders of the path are God’s limits. No one falls within those limits. God until the veil of God is revealed, and the one above whom he calls is the exhorter of God Almighty.”"
"10720","I am Ahmad bin Suleiman, we are Affan bin Muslim, we are Hammad bin Salamah, I am Thabit, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Suhaib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read this verse: “For those who do good, goodness and more.” He said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, And the people of Hell are Hell. A herald called out: O people of Paradise, indeed you have a promise from your Lord that He wants to fulfill for you. They said: Didn’t he make it white? Our faces, and He makes our scales heavy, and He admits us to Paradise, and He saves us from Hell. He said: Then He will remove the veil, and they will look at Him. By God, what is it? God gave them something more beloved to them than looking at Him, and something more pleasing to their eyes.”"
"10721","I am Hafs bin Omar, we are Muhammad bin Saeed bin Sabiq, on the authority of Ya’qub, and Ibrahim bin Yaqoub informed us, we are Uthman bin Zufar, we are Ya’qub, On the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was asked, and Abraham said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked. May God bless him and grant him peace: Who are God’s saints? He said: “Those who, when they see, remember God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10722","I am Wasil bin Abdul-Ala, I am Muhammad bin Fudayl, on the authority of his father, and Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, among the servants are servants whom the prophets and martyrs envy.” It was said: Who are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “They are a people who loved each other in the spirit of God, without wealth or lineage. Their faces are light, that is, on platforms of light. They do not fear if people fear. And they do not grieve if the people grieve. Then he recited this verse: “Indeed, the guardians of God have no fear, nor do they grieve.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10723","I am Ziyad bin Ayyub, from Hushaym, from Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came In Medina, he found the Jews fasting on the day of Ashura. They were asked about that, and they said: This is the day on which God revealed Moses and his sons. Israel is against Pharaoh, and we fast in honor of him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have more right to Moses than you,” and he commanded “By his fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10724","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, we are Muhammad bin Ja’far, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. On the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, one of them referred it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “The Gabriel used to put clay in Pharaoh's mouth for fear that he would say: There is no god but God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10725","I am Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid, we are Ali bin Ayyash, we are Shuaib, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what Abdul Rahman Al-Araj told him, from what He mentioned that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating it, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The right hand of God is full, it cannot be disturbed by any expenditure.” the night and the day.” And He said: “Have you seen what He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? For He has not spent what is in His right hand, and His throne is over the water.” And in his other hand is the scales, lowering and raising.”"
